Multiply the matrix by the column of coordinates, taking each row against the column. For $\mathbf M=\begin{pmatrix}1&0&2\\0&2&1\\1&1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and the point $(2,-1,3)$:

$$
\begin{pmatrix}1&0&2\\0&2&1\\1&1&0\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}2\\-1\\3\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}2+0+6\\0-2+3\\2-1+0\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}8\\1\\1\end{pmatrix}
\tag{4}
$$

so the image is $(8,1,1)$. The first column of $\mathbf M$ is the image of $(1,0,0)$, the second of $(0,1,0)$ and the third of $(0,0,1)$. Combined transformations are again multiplied with the first one on the right.
